### Test results
- `python -m pytest tests` → 137 passed (31 new; 106 → 137).
- Coverage (`--cov=anvil_runtime`): 94% overall. API package ≈98% — routes_runs 98%,
  routes_events 100%, routes_artifacts 98%, routes_health 100%, deps 93% (get_secret_adapter
  exercised in Slice 5), app.py 100%, secret_adapter 100% (≥80% API / ≥70% overall met).
- TypeScript: NOT RUN — Node.js/npm unavailable (Slice 1 carry-forward). The two
  vitest suites are written to spec and run wherever Node is present.

### Design decisions (within blueprint/spec, no drift)
- Orchestration over HTTP is synchronous and deterministic: state-changing routes
  (start, granted approval, force-advance, rollback) drive `run_until_pause` so the
  supervisor advances to the next gate/escalation/stop/completion before responding.
  A denied approval and `stop` deliberately do not advance.
- SSE route replays the run's persisted event snapshot (`EventBus.stream`) then
  closes — deterministic and TestClient-friendly. Live tailing via `EventBus.subscribe`
  is a later iteration on the same contract; the app shares one EventBus between the
  supervisor and the stream route so they cannot diverge.
- `/v1/health` honestly reports `config: ok` and `mcp_discovery/openhands: pending`
  (Slice 5 subsystems) rather than faking the blueprint's all-`ok` illustrative example;
  overall status is `ok` unless a check is `error`.
- `/v1/artifacts/{phase}` resolves the phase's first file-shaped `allowed_output` from
  PHASE_CONTRACTS; directory-only phases (e.g. implementation→src/) and ungenerated
  artifacts return 404.
- TS request/response/event interfaces and helper types (FetchLike, SseDecoder,
  ChatCommand, EventPresentation, etc.) are colocated inside their assigned matrix
  modules — no new module files introduced (same approach as Slices 2/3).

### Issues encountered and fixes
- routes_artifacts initially at 40% line coverage (only the unknown-phase 404 was
  tested). Added tests/integration/api/test_artifacts_endpoint.py covering the happy
  path + the directory-only and not-generated 404 branches → ≈98%. No functional changes.
- All Python suites passed on the first full run after authoring; no retries needed.

### Drift check (against blueprint / architecture / spec)
- Modules created == the Slice-4 rows of the plan §8 assignment matrix
  (app.py; api/{deps,routes_runs,routes_events,routes_artifacts,routes_health};
  security/secret_adapter; extension chat/runtime/ui/secrets/telemetry modules).
  No unmapped source modules.
- extension/src/extension.ts (a Slice 1 module) was MODIFIED to register the chat
  participant — explicitly anticipated by the Slice 1 scaffold's own comments and
  plan §2.1; this is planned activation wiring, not drift. The protected shared
  contract files (phase_contracts.py, api/models.py, config/schema.py) were consumed,
  not modified.
- Endpoints, request/response shapes, and constants match blueprint §5.1/§6.2 and
  api/models.py verbatim. No drift detected.

### Carry-forward
- TypeScript build/test still require Node.js (Slice 1 carry-forward), now covering
  the full extension client and its two vitest suites. Run before final sign-off.
- The secret adapter and policy/hook engines are reachable but not yet on the
  execution path; LLM/tool dispatch wiring is Slice 5 (sdk/* + llm/* + tools/*).
- Live SSE tailing (vs. snapshot replay) is a non-blocking enhancement on the
  existing EventBus.subscribe contract.

